<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy sets 3.0 billion mark repo tender.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy sets 3.0 billion mark repo tender.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it called a one-month 3.0 billion mark repurchase tender for Thursday February 13 for government securities to be resold on March 18, renewing a similar amount expiring.</p>
<p>At a previous one-month foreign currency operation for 3.0 billion marks on January 14, the minimum accepted rate stood at 7.34 percent and the average rate at 7.36 percent.</p>
